        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: радость",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "радость (rádost) — \"joy\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "радость (rádost) is рад, \"glad\", with -ость, the suffix that makes nouns of quality. рад goes back to Proto-Slavic radŭ; Vasmer finds a link with Old English rōt, \"cheerful\", likely, but reports a rival account."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
