          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "грусть (grust) goes with the verb грустить, \"to be sad\". Vasmer reports the usual link with груда, \"a heap\", and with Lithuanian graudùs, \"brittle; sad, moving\", from a root \"to crush\" (Lithuanian grūsti, \"to pound\"). Vasmer himself thinks a link with the verb \"to gnaw\" more likely: a sadness that gnaws."
            }
          ]
